<title>UK: GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greg Norman consolidated his</p>
<p>position at the head of the world golf rankings after winning</p>
<p>the Australian Open for the fifth time at the weekend.</p>
<p>Paul Stankowski, playoff winner in the Casio World Open, has</p>
<p>moved up to 57th position .</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p> 1. Greg Norman (Australia)	  10.41 points</p>
<p> 2. Tom Lehman			    9.65</p>
<p> 3. Nick Faldo (Britain)		8.85</p>
<p> 4. Ernie Els (South Africa)	  8.73</p>
<p> 5. Fred Couples			  8.55</p>
<p> 6. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)     8.31</p>
<p> 7. Phil Mickelson			7.85</p>
<p> 8. Davis Love III			7.53</p>
<p> 9. Corey Pavin			   7.46</p>
<p> 10. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	    7.45</p>
<p> 11. Mark O'Meara			 7.10</p>
<p> 12. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	    6.18</p>
<p> 13. Steve Stricker		     6.11</p>
<p> 14. Steve Elkington (Australia)    5.91</p>
<p> 15. Bernhard Langer (Germany)	5.64</p>
<p> 16. Scott Hoch			   5.56</p>
<p> 17. Tom Watson			   5.28</p>
<p> 18. Loren Roberts			5.20</p>
<p> 19. David Dubal			  5.19</p>
<p> 20. Mark Brooks			  5.18</p>
